---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Draft terms for using and sharing the educational content on Psychology Blog."
>
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Using this website</p><h1>
        A few shared expectations.
      </h1><p>Last updated 6 November 2026.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="callout">
        These are draft terms. The site owner, legal identity, contact details,
        rights ownership, and applicable law need confirmation and legal review
        before public launch.
      </p>
      <h2>Educational use</h2><p>
        You may read and link to the site's articles for general information.
        Please read the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> to understand the limits
        of this material. The site does not offer personal care, crisis response,
        or professional advice.
      </p>
      <h2>Sharing the content</h2><p>
        Links to the original pages are welcome. If you want to reproduce an
        article, publish a translation, or use substantial parts of the content,
        seek permission from the confirmed rights holder. A permission contact
        and licensing details have not yet been supplied.
      </p>
      <h2>Respectful use</h2><p>
        Do not use the site to distribute malicious material, disrupt its
        availability, misrepresent the source of content, or attempt
        unauthorized access. There are no reader accounts or comment features in
        this version.
      </p>
      <h2>Accuracy and changes</h2><p>
        Articles and pages may be edited, moved, or removed. We aim to correct
        errors, but the current content is sample material awaiting review. A
        date on an article is not a guarantee that every linked resource remains
        current.
      </p>
      <h2>Other services</h2><p>
        External websites, newsletter providers, and media platforms have their
        own terms. Review those terms when you choose to use a linked service.
        The blog does not control those services.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2><p>
        See <a href="/contact/">contact availability</a> for the current status of
        the owner's contact channel. No specific jurisdiction, dispute process, or
        legal waiver is asserted by this draft.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
